    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen managing multi-user systems as root, logging in as a different user means losing all neovim plugins. Whilst it’s possible to install system-wide plugins into `/usr/local/share/nvim/site/pack/plugins`, such plugins can’t be upgraded by `vim.pack`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt’d be really nice for root users to be able to manage system-wide neovim plugins using `vim.pack`.",
