        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It’d be really nice for root users to be able to manage system-wide neovim plugins using `vim.pack`.\n\nIt is still possible to install and manage plugins with `vim.pack` under root. They are installed inside `data` directory (see it with `:=vim.fn.stdpath('data')`) with a regular `vim.pack.add({ ... })` call (I've just confirmed it locally). The final path for a single plugin for me was `/root/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/plugin_name`.\n\nCould you please elaborate on what is the problem here? Is it that `vim.pack.update()` doesn't work? If that that is the case, did you run it as a super-user?\n\n",
