        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Whilst it’s possible to install system-wide plugins into `/usr/local/share/nvim/site/pack/plugins`, such plugins can’t be upgraded by `vim.pack`.\n\nSure they can, if you run as root and set 'packpath' appropriately.\n\nBut I'm *guessing* what is requested here is a way for `vim.pack` to source its plugins from >=2 locations, i.e. instead of a single root `~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/core/` , you want vim.pack to look into 2 places?\n\nWouldn't it work (and seems ergonomic to me), for your system admin to \"host\" a local git repo(s), then users can do this in their configs:\n\n```lua\nvim.pack.add{\n  'file://path/to/root-owned-1.git',\n  'file://path/to/root-owned-2.git',\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nAnd you can automatically add that to user configs via `:h system-vimrc`.",
