        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Thank you very much for the explanations. Our specific situation is a system that's mostly used by the sysadmin, but where the sysadmin needs to perform work by logging into different accounts and launch neovim there.\n\nOur problem is we're trying to migrate from our previously installed plugins repos without adding to vim.lua.\n\nBefore 0.12, we put the repos in `/usr/local/share/nvim/site/pack/plugins/start`. Am I correct in thinking that it's just not possible to tell `vim.pack` to 'pick up' such existing repos with a simlink like this:\n\n```sh\n$ export XDG_DATA_HOME=\"/usr/local/share\"\n$ ln -s /usr/local/share/nvim/site/pack/plugins/start /usr/local/share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt\n```\n\nand that the only way to migrate is to remove the old repos and write the relevant GitHub links in vim.lua?",
